{"hw":"τῷ","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">τῷ</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">τῷ</span>, dat. sg. neut. of <span class=\"lex-gram\">ὁ</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ἡ</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">τό</span>, used abs., <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">therefore, in this wise, then,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hom.</span> </span>, <abbr>v.</abbr> <span class=\"lex-gram\">ὁ</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ἡ</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">τό</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> </span> VIII. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2</span> </span> a, b; <span class=\"gk\">ἀλλ' οὔτε περισπᾶται οὔτε σὺν τῷ ι γράφεται</span> (i.e. <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">τώ</span>) <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.D.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Adv.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">199.2</span> </span>: written <span class=\"gk\">τὼ</span> in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Alc.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Supp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">26.11</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> <span class=\"gk\">τῷ;</span> for <span class=\"gk\">τίνι;</span> dat. sg. of <span class=\"gk\">τίς;</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">who?</b> but </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> <span class=\"gk\">τῳ,</span> enclit. for <span class=\"gk\">τινί,</span> dat. sg. of <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">τις</span>, <b class=\"lex-tr\">some one.</b> </div></div>"}